.TH install 1 "June 21, 2026" "install 202606022117-git" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
install \- self-hosted Quay registry stack installer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B install.sh
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-\-color=auto|yes|no\fR]
[\fB\-\-debug\fR]
[\fB\-\-remove\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Self-hosted Quay registry stack installer. Sets up Quay, Postgres, Redis, and Clair under /opt/quay.
Detects available container engines (docker/podman), probes SMTP availability, generates secrets,
and brings up the complete registry stack. Idempotent — safe to run multiple times; existing secrets
and database data are preserved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-color=auto|yes|no
Color output control. Auto: detect TTY and respect NO_COLOR env var; yes: force color on; no: force color off (same as setting NO_COLOR).
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable debug mode (set -x).
.TP
.BR \-\-remove
Stop all containers and delete /opt/quay (destructive).
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B DOMAIN
Registry hostname (e.g., registry.example.com). If not set, auto-detected from hostname command.
Must be a valid registerable domain. Required for operation.
.TP
.B APP_ADMIN_USER
Superuser account username created on first run.
Default: administrator
.TP
.B APP_ADMIN_PASS
Superuser account password. Auto-generated (24 random chars) if not set.
Store securely; never saved in logs.
.TP
.B REGISTRY_TITLE
Full display name shown in the registry UI.
Default: Quay
.TP
.B REGISTRY_TITLE_SHORT
Short name shown in the browser tab.
Default: value of REGISTRY_TITLE
.TP
.B QUAY_IMAGE
Quay container image to deploy. Automatically resolves to the latest stable release if not set.
Default: quay.io/projectquay/quay:3.17.2 (or detected latest)
.TP
.B CLAIR_IMAGE
Clair (security scanner) container image. Automatically resolves to the latest stable release if not set.
Default: quay.io/projectquay/clair:4.9.0 (or detected latest)
.TP
.B TZ
Timezone for all containers (IANA format).
Default: America/New_York
.TP
.B SMTP_HOST
SMTP server hostname for outbound email. Auto-detected as the Docker bridge IP if not set.
.TP
.B SMTP_PORT
SMTP server port.
Default: 25
.TP
.B SMTP_ENABLED
Whether to enable email notifications. Auto-probed on each run (never loaded from .env).
Set to "true" or "false". Unset to enable auto-detection.
.TP
.B QUAY_BIND_ADDR
Address to bind Quay's HTTP port. Auto-detected from container bridge network if not set.
Default: 0.0.0.0 (or detected bridge IP)
.TP
.B QUAY_PORT
Port for Quay's HTTP endpoint. Auto-selected from 62000-64999 range on first run; persisted thereafter.
.TP
.B HOST_IP_4
Container-to-host reachability IP for SMTP and other services.
Default: 172.17.0.1 (or auto-detected from interface)
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /opt/quay/.env
Single environment file containing all generated secrets, credentials, and runtime configuration.
Mode 600 (readable by owner only). Never committed to version control.
.TP
.B /opt/quay/docker-compose.yml
Docker Compose manifest for quay-app, quay-db, quay-redis, and quay-clair services.
Regenerated on each run to refresh bind addresses and port settings.
.TP
.B /opt/quay/bin/quay-gc.sh
Wrapper script for daily garbage collection. Automatically scheduled via systemd timer or cron.
.TP
.B /opt/quay/bin/quay-verify-user.sh
Helper to mark a Quay user account as email-verified directly in PostgreSQL.
Useful when SMTP is disabled and a user is stuck on the activation screen.
.TP
.B /opt/quay/volumes/
All runtime data: database files, container logs, image storage, configuration, and credentials.
Persisted across restarts and re-runs.
.TP
.B /opt/quay/volumes/config/quay/stack/config.yaml
Quay configuration file. Contains feature flags, branding, security settings, and database/Redis addresses.
Regenerated on each run (configuration; persistent state lives in the database).
.TP
.B /opt/quay/volumes/config/clair/config.yaml
Clair v4 configuration. Contains database connection strings for the security scanner.
Regenerated on each run.
.TP
.B /opt/quay/volumes/config/credentials/cosign.{key,pub}
Ed25519 keypair for container image signing (cosign). Generated on first run if openssl or cosign is available.
.TP
.B /etc/systemd/system/quay-gc.timer
Systemd timer triggering daily garbage collection at 03:00 local time (if systemd is available).
.TP
.B /etc/cron.d/quay-gc
Fallback cron job for garbage collection (used if systemd is not available).
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
Requires at least one of:
.RS
.IP "•" 3
Docker with Docker Compose plugin or standalone docker-compose binary
.IP "•" 3
Podman with podman-compose
.RE
.TP
Also requires:
.RS
.IP "•" 3
curl (for image version discovery and health checks)
.IP "•" 3
Standard POSIX tools: sh, awk, grep, tr, dd
.IP "•" 3
ss or netstat (for port availability checking)
.IP "•" 3
curl or nc (for SMTP detection)
.IP "•" 3
(optional) openssl or cosign (for Ed25519 keypair generation; script warns if absent)
.RE
.SH BEHAVIOR
.TP
.B Idempotent
Safe to run multiple times on the same host. Existing secrets, database data, and container volumes persist.
Configuration files are refreshed on each run; application state lives in the database.
.TP
.B SMTP Auto-Detection
Probes port 25 (or SMTP_PORT) on first run and each subsequent run. Sets SMTP_ENABLED accordingly.
Containers reach host SMTP via the Docker bridge IP (HOST_IP_4).
.TP
.B Secrets Persistence
Generated on first run: database passwords, admin account credentials, Quay secret key, cosign keypair.
Stored in /opt/quay/.env (mode 600). Reused on re-runs; never overwritten unless explicitly unset.
.TP
.B Port Selection
Quay HTTP port auto-selected from 62000-64999 range on first run. Persisted to .env.
Binding address auto-detected from Docker/Podman bridge network.
.TP
.B Image Resolution
Fetches latest stable (x.y.z) release tags from Quay's API if QUAY_IMAGE/CLAIR_IMAGE not set.
Falls back to known-good pinned versions on network failure or empty tag list.
.TP
.B Superuser Auto-Creation
On first run, creates the superuser account (APP_ADMIN_USER) via Quay's registration API.
Marks account verified directly in PostgreSQL so email verification does not block login,
regardless of SMTP configuration.
.TP
.B Garbage Collection
Systemd timer (preferred) or cron job runs daily at 03:00 local time.
Executes Quay's internal garbage-collect and manage gc commands.
Stale locks (>2h) are cleaned up automatically.
.SH SECURITY NOTES
.TP
.B Secrets
Admin password and all database credentials are printed once to stdout at the end of installation.
Never appear in logs thereafter. Store securely.
.TP
.B TLS
Quay expects TLS to be terminated upstream by a reverse proxy.
Direct IP:port access works for health checks and web UI; bearer auth challenges redirect clients to HTTPS domain.
.TP
.B Credential Files
cosign.key is mode 600 (owner only). Database credentials are embedded in config files (mode 640/660).
Never committed to version control.
.TP
.B Umask
Script sets umask 077 — all generated files are non-world-readable by default.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Install with defaults and auto-detect domain:
.RS
sudo sh install.sh
.RE
.TP
.B Specify registry domain and admin user:
.RS
sudo DOMAIN=registry.example.com APP_ADMIN_USER=admin sh install.sh
.RE
.TP
.B Specify custom titles and disable color in summary:
.RS
sudo REGISTRY_TITLE="My Registry" REGISTRY_TITLE_SHORT="Mine" sh install.sh --color=no
.RE
.TP
.B Check version:
.RS
sh install.sh --version
.RE
.TP
.B View help:
.RS
sh install.sh --help
.RE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
On failure, the script exits with status 1 and prints an ERROR message with timestamp.
Common issues:
.TP
.B "Missing required command"
Install docker (or podman), docker-compose (or podman-compose), and curl.
.TP
.B "Docker is installed but Docker Compose not found"
Install docker-compose plugin: `docker compose version` or standalone package.
.TP
.B "DOMAIN must be a valid registerable domain"
Set DOMAIN to a valid DNS name (e.g., DOMAIN=registry.example.com sh install.sh).
.TP
.B "Image pull failed"
Verify QUAY_IMAGE and CLAIR_IMAGE are reachable and correct.
Check network connectivity and image registry credentials (docker login).
.TP
.B "Quay did not become healthy within 300 s"
First boot requires database migration. Check logs:
.RS
docker compose -f /opt/quay/docker-compose.yml -e /opt/quay/.env logs quay-app
.RE
